					"uidString" : "lNc8bTyZDQCZnYokDqn2mw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "This database is a booklet about my journey of adding support for [Carp](https://github.com/carp-lang/carp) to the Glamorous Toolkit. It may also serve as an instructional text for others who may wish to add language support for a language of their choice to the Glamorous Toolkit."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2022-04-17T16:49:06.977343+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2022-04-17T16:49:10.770322+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "i6aBezyZDQCZo8ldDqn2mw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "### My why"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2022-04-17T16:46:59.7649+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2022-04-17T16:48:57.270379+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "CvfjczyZDQCZnkdvDqn2mw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "When I set out on this adventure, I wanted to build an IDE for Carp. I thought that building an IDE for a language that has **syntactic macros**, **type inference**, and **borrow checking** might be an interesting undertaking. Helping a user navigate the process of writing macros and helping them debug them, showing types and lifetimes at every point in their program, seemed like an interesting idea worth exploring."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2022-04-17T16:48:58.594533+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2022-04-17T16:49:05.117045+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "UC7/ejyZDQCZovUTDqn2mw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "It also seemed like a daunting idea."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2022-04-17T16:49:19.287082+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:45:39.487355+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "yNw0fDyZDQCZpDnKDqn2mw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "I had never built an IDE. When I wrote the first version of this booklet in 2022, I had been involved in building and maintaining the Glamorous Toolkit for over half a year. Before that, I mostly worked on language internals."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2022-04-17T16:50:19.582232+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:45:39.487355+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "zXPVfzyZDQCZpT4hDqn2mw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "Maybe that blend of knowing the internals of Carp and the Glamorous Toolkit helped, but I found that with the help of the Toolkit, I was able to build something resembling an IDE in a few afternoons. After that, it sat mostly untouched for a few years. In 2026 I came back to it with a compiler that can stay alive between inputs, and it grew into something much closer to what I had in mind."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2022-04-17T16:51:18.544965+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2022-04-17T16:51:22.163297+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "hFxOgzyZDQCZpvYADqn2mw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "### Our Journey"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2022-04-17T16:51:28.559246+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:45:39.487355+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "W1+ogzyZDQCZp7heDqn2mw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "This booklet has two parts. In the first, I will go through the process of adding language support step by step. We will build a parser and play around with it for a bit. We will add a highlighter and marvel at how prettily it renders our code. We will build a way to execute code, and a snippet type, so we can write and run Carp from directly within Lepiter. That part should be useful for whatever language you want to bring into GT."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "tUpqzNHHRe2oIlcD/SjFvw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "The second part is about what gt4carp does today, and how. Once the compiler can answer questions about a program instead of just running it, the IDE gets to show a lot more: types, diagnostics, macro expansions, live values, a native debugger, and a project browser. That part is more specific to Carp, but I think most of the ideas carry over to any language with a compiler you can talk to."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "carpSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2022-08-21T13:26:14.248045+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:45:39.487355+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "sEr+VSCjDQCp+CTdALqe5Q=="
				},
				"code" : "; this is what we will be able to do\r(defn twice [x] (* x 2))\r(twice 21)"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
